<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="https://de-tu-dresden-inf-lat.github.io/evee/cd.owl#"
     xml:base="https://de-tu-dresden-inf-lat.github.io/evee/cd.owl"
     xmlns:cd="http://tu-dresden.de/inf/lat/evee/cd#"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://de-tu-dresden-inf-lat.github.io/evee/cd.owl">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The annotation properties with which an OWL EL ontology states constraints of a concrete domain for the reasoner PACER of Evee (https://github.com/de-tu-dresden-inf-lat/evee), and the names of the concrete domains. Importing this ontology is optional: it only declares and describes these names.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PACER annotations</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Annotation properties
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->


    


    <!-- http://tu-dresden.de/inf/lat/evee/cd#concreteDomain -->


    <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://tu-dresden.de/inf/lat/evee/cd#concreteDomain">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Ontology annotation that names the concrete domain of the constraints: cd:QDiff, cd:QMult or cd:QLinear, or one of the strings &quot;QDiff&quot;, &quot;QMult&quot; and &quot;QLinear&quot;. An ontology without it uses the concrete domain that its imports name, if they agree; if no ontology names one, PACER reasons like ELK.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">concrete domain</rdfs:label>
    </owl:AnnotationProperty>
    


    <!-- http://tu-dresden.de/inf/lat/evee/cd#constraint -->


    <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://tu-dresden.de/inf/lat/evee/cd#constraint">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Annotation of a class with a constraint, written as a string: the class stands for the elements whose data property values satisfy the constraint. A class has at most one constraint; constraints are combined by intersections of their classes (ObjectIntersectionOf). Data properties are written as prefixed names with the prefixes of the ontology (:age), as full IRIs in angle brackets, or as plain names in the default namespace. Numbers are decimals (0.5, 1e-3) or fractions (1/3), and are treated exactly. def(x) says that x has a value. Which other constraints can be written depends on the concrete domain; see cd:QDiff, cd:QMult and cd:QLinear.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">constraint</rdfs:label>
    </owl:AnnotationProperty>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Annotations
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->


    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://tu-dresden.de/inf/lat/evee/cd#QDiff">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The rational numbers with the constraints x = c, x &gt; c, x + c = y and x - c = y, and def(x), where x and y are data properties and c is a number. Examples: :age &gt; 17, :end - 2 = :start.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">QDiff</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://tu-dresden.de/inf/lat/evee/cd#QLinear">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The rational numbers with linear equations a1 * x1 + ... + an * xn = c, and def(x), where x1, ..., xn are different data properties and a1, ..., an and c are numbers. A coefficient 1 can be omitted, and - subtracts. Examples: :water + :milk - :total = 0, 0.5 * :x - :y = 1.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">QLinear</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://tu-dresden.de/inf/lat/evee/cd#QMult">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The rational numbers, including 0 and the negative numbers, with the constraints x = c, x &lt; c and c * x = y (also written x * c = y) for a factor c &gt; 0, and def(x), where x and y are data properties and c is a number. Examples: :weight &lt; 80, 2 * :radius = :diameter.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">QMult</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
</rdf:RDF>



